<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-10976] MVCC: Sql API methods should throw proper TransactionExceptions in case of tx failure.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10976</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;For now Sql API can throws&#160;SqlException (without any actual Tx failure cause) or TransactionException wrapped into CacheException.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also, I&apos;ve found we convert unchecked exceptions into checked ones and then back without any obvious reason.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let&apos;s make TransactionException thows properly and add it to Sql Api contract.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
